            <ArticleTitle>[Characteristics of cardiac regulation in ischemic damage to the ventricular myocardium].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>409-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The evoked potentials produced by the irritation of the heart sinus node zone in the brain cortex and bradycardia have been registered in 5 to 40-min ischemia of the left and right ventricular myocardium during the electrical stimulation of the vagus. Restricted cardiac afferentation and the heart escape from vagus influences have been revealed at the early stages of ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
